# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.14.1 - Identify and correct system flaws timely
# Platform: M365 (Intune managed devices)
# Check type: m365_graph_query against /deviceManagement/managedDevices

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-14-1-m365-flaw-remediation-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `m365`
    criticality `high`

    title `CMMC L1 SI.L1-3.14.1: Identify, report, and correct information system flaws`
    description `Validates that managed devices are reporting compliance to the device management plane. The Intune managed-device inventory is the evidence surface for ongoing flaw identification - devices that fail to report or that report non-compliant trigger remediation workflows.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `m365,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-14-1,si,flaw-remediation,intune,managed-devices`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.14.1`
    control_objective `3.14.1`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `M365:tenant:endpoint-management`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Ensure every managed device is enrolled in Intune and reports compliance state on a recurring sync. Investigate any device reporting noncompliant or with a stale lastSyncDateTime; remediate the underlying flaw or quarantine the device pending remediation.`

    component_id `comp-m365-endpoint`

    impl_3_14_1 `Information system flaws are identified and corrected in a timely manner through device-management telemetry. All endpoints in the boundary are enrolled in centralized device management; each device transmits a compliance state and an audit-friendly sync timestamp on a recurring interval. Devices reporting noncompliant or stale state trigger remediation workflows that either remotely correct the flaw (patch, configuration push) or block the device from accessing organizational resources until corrected. The compliance state is consulted by Conditional Access policies at sign-in time, enforcing remediation as a precondition for resource access.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT managed_devices
        path `deviceManagement/managedDevices`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE devices_reporting_compliance
        found boolean = true
        record
            field rows.*.complianceState string != `` at_least_one
            field rows.*.lastSyncDateTime string != `` at_least_one
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN m365_graph_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF devices_reporting_compliance
            OBJECT_REF managed_devices
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
